      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description:\n\n[Shot 1] preserve the exact visual composition established by <Picture 1>. A woman wearing a white astronaut suit is floating outside a large spacecraft in space. Her body is positioned diagonally in the frame, with one hand holding the spacecraft's exterior structure while a thick flexible safety tether connects her suit to the spacecraft. The spacecraft fills much of the background, with Earth visible below and deep black space with distant stars behind her. The woman and spacecraft remain visually consistent with the reference image. The camera holds the exterior medium-wide framing with subtle floating movement.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the thick safety tether suddenly breaks free from its attachment point on the spacecraft. The broken tether recoils and drifts away while the woman loses her connection to the spacecraft. She slowly begins drifting away from the spacecraft in zero gravity, no longer anchored to it. The spacecraft remains in the background as the distance between the woman and the spacecraft gradually increases.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.000, the camera cuts to a close-up of the woman's face inside her astronaut helmet. She realizes that the tether has broken and that she is drifting away from the spacecraft. Her eyes widen and her facial expression changes to fear and panic. She looks back toward the spacecraft while continuing to float weightlessly.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nThe quiet ambient hum of the spacecraft, subtle astronaut breathing and spacesuit sounds, followed by a sharp mechanical snap as the tether breaks. After the break, the environment becomes quiet again with tense breathing inside the helmet.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA subtle low-frequency cinematic tension begins as the tether breaks and gradually intensifies during the close-up of the frightened astronaut.",
        1344,
        768,
        124
      ]
